he  jagers to tear it down putting the  alliance in a very delicate situation if  they make a wrong move then their one  method of reaching aaron will disappear  so whatever strategy they choose it  basically needs to be perfect when it  comes to annie her suggestion was to  quickly massacre the enemy in one go by  using the combined power of their titan  shifters and other weapons  if successful it would mean that the  jagrus would be wiped out before they  have a chance to destroy the ship but  this plan caused the scouts to hesitate  for obvious reasons  many of the people defending the poor  are friends they've known since all the  way back in their cadets and connie  especially didn't seem comfortable with  killing them on top of that mikasa  highlights that an all-out attack would  also lead to the azmobito getting hurt  which is something that can't be allowed  to happen besides the fact that they're  her distant relatives the azimibito need  to be kept safe because they're the only  ones who can prepare the flying boats  onyankpon goes on to explain that  although he has the skills to pilot the  plane his ruse engineers are the ones  with the knowledge on how to prepare it  for flight and without them it won't be  able to get in the air  therefore the alliance had to think of a  plan that would prevent the boat from  getting destroyed while giving the  engineers time to set it up while also  hordes of viegras might be trying to  kill them by itself that mission would  be difficult enough but the fact that  scouts want to do it without causing  deaths makes it virtually impossible  annie then throws some shader arm in by  asking him to tell her his grand plan  just like he did 4 years ago when he  lured her into a trap  on that occasion he told her a  completely fake plan in the hopes that  she'd follow him underground however in  the present day he doesn't seem too  proud about what he did and in my  opinion it's because seeing berto's  memories and you know seeing things from  the warriors perspective it's made him  empathize with what they had to go  through  anyway soon after this connie has an  outburst as he's still not on board with  the prospect of killing his fellow  islanders which causes annie to come to  a realization although the warriors  might have an obligation to save their  homelands from being trampled the scouts  never had this burden and they shouldn't  be forced to murder their own people if  they don't want to she goes on to say  that if these four have been in the same  position as the warriors then they  wouldn't have attacked the walls and  started this whole war between marley  and paradise  these words caused reiner to recall what  eren said to him back in liberio and  i'll explain why he thinks of that in  this moment  if we flash back to the whole scene  reiner had just admitted that annie and  berto wanted to end the mission but he's  the one who convinced them to keep going  and attack war maria in aaron's mind  this confirmed to him that he and rhino  were the same since they each pushed  forward to wipe out their enemies even  when the people around them were against  it  in both situations they dragged their  comrades along to help put an end to  countless lives and in the present day  reiner makes the decision that he  doesn't want to drag any more people  into this conflict he tells connie and  the rest of them that they don't need to  interfere with this upcoming battle and  urges them to stay behind and watch the  fighting from a distance  now moving on earlier in the episode  hanji noticed something about the  rumbling that made her stand up and take  a look what's happening here is that the  war titans have entered the water and  are now swimming to mali and because  they're so hot the water begins to emit  steam the steam gives a clear indication  of how fast the titans are moving and  based on this hanji estimates that some  of the titans have already arrived on  the continent  this means that towns and cities to the  northeast of mali have almost certainly  been trampled and the news causes mcgath  to take immediate action  pushing on yankopono out the way he  shoves the other net against the rock  and stomps her arm into a different  dimension the general covers her mouth  so that her scream doesn't draw any  attention and the reason he's torturing  her is so that she'll tell him where the  founding titan is  even though her will to live was pretty  low before this the way things have  progressed have made her interested to  see how this all plays out and in the  end she basically says that she'll tell  them his location if they bring her  along  following that macathan looks up at  gabby and has a clear look of regret on  his face similar to what happened the  night before  back then he went to reach out to her  because he felt guilty about the fact  that marley's brainwashing had robbed  her of a normal childhood and this is  the case not just for gabby but for  rainer and the other warriors as well as  the head of the unit mcgath played a  significant role in making this happen  and here he apologizes for the things he  said around the campfire the argument he  had with jon was simply him trying to  justify his own actions because deep  down he knew that both himself and  marley were awful for the things they've  done  last night he was too afraid to accept  that which is why he put his hand down  but after seeing the things he's seen  his perspective on aldians in the world  has now evolved that being said the  general does still want to stop aaron  not only to save mali but also so that  future generations can learn about their  mistakes it's interesting that when he  talks about future generations learning  their history the anime pans to show us  yellen his expression as her motivation  for helping zeke and lying about her  heritage was so that she could be part  of a legend that future generations  would hear about  meanwhile down by the harbour flock was  seemingly having the happiest day of his  life as he observed the wall titans  rapidly pacing towards the globe  he explains to kyomi that his rule will  be trampled just like all the other  nations which i thought was a bit harsh  considering that they were the one  country who were actually willing to  work with paradise if anyone was going  to be spared it would have been them but  this line is basically a confirmation  that aaron really is taking no prisoners  anyhow in this scene we can see that  kyomi wasn't his only hostage as there  was a room full of terrified engineers  at least three of whom had been killed  already flock previously mentioned that  one of his main jobs is to wipe out any  resentment left on the island and so  he's taking the same approach with his  uru as he did with the volunteers that  approach is that anyone who doesn't do  what they're told or tries to resist is  executed while everyone else will be  allowed to live if they're willing to  contribute to elder going forward  as he continues to ramble kyomi then  interrupts him and tells flock that the  violence won't end even once owners  wiped out the rest of humanity we know  for a fact that what she's saying is  true because even before mali first  attacked there was still a ton of  bloodshed on the island whether it was  state-sponsored executions serial  killers on the loose or political  assassinations gyomi's opinion is that  it's pretty much human nature for these  things to continue like they always have  and he even accepts that she does have a  point he goes on to say however that  what's important now is for people to  know their place in the world and that  was a thinly veiled warning to everyone  in the room  essentially he's acknowledging that  their society on parodies is more  primitive compared to the rest of the  world and that while it would be nice to  have hizrus tech it's not essential for  their survival in that way he's telling  kiyomi that he's not afraid to kill them  and that the azimobito clan need to do  what they're told if they want to live  despite all of their technological  advancements in the new world the eren  is creating their place is now below the  aegirus and this is what he's trying to  make her realize  suddenly out of nowhere connie and armin  interrupt this conversation as they ride  into the harbor on horseback and this  was the beginning of their plan to get  to the flying boat without killing  anyone phase one of this plan involves  convincing jaegers that they're all  still on the same side and to do that he  claims that they've been chasing after  the warriors this whole time and now the  armored and cart tyson have escaped by  sea the implication here is that flock  needs to let them use the flying boat so  that they can continue chasing after the  enemy and for that reason they also need  to let the azmobito prepare the flight  he and connie then rush towards the  plane while telling flock to release the  mechanics and as they get closer we see  it's being guarded by daz and samuel  these four have all known each other  since they first joined the cadets and  daz in particular is memorable for being  the most anxious and possibly the most  useless of the entire group  regardless of that he and samuel are now  both proud jaegerys who are fully in  support of aaron's plan to rumble all  life beyond the walls it was them who  rigged this flying boat with explosives  in case he needed to be destroyed  causing armor and connie to hysterically  ask them to disconnect it  in this scene you can tell that samuel  is hesitant to do that since there are  suspicions among the aegiris that these  two are working with mali flock first  began to suspect this when mikasa and  the rest of them went missing but after  a brief back and forth dad is eventually  convinced to disconnect the detonator  with the explosives now being inactive  the two of them have an almost terrified  look on their face and that's because  during this whole interaction they were  nervous that their plan wouldn't work  inside the building though flock's  suspicion continued to grow as he began  to poke holes in armin's story when the  two scouts arrived they claimed that the  warriors were heading south so logically  if armin knew that then it would have  made more sense to pursue them by train  rather than on horses the events of the  last episode demonstrated just how much  more effective that would have been and  there's also the fact that the scouts  were sneaking around without asking any  of the aegis for help  even though he had no evidence that  they'd been betrayed his inescapable gut  feeling was that something was wrong so  to deal with this he decides to execute  more of the remaining mechanics  a second meaning we can draw from this  moment is that in flock's mind even if  armin's story is true he doesn't think  the warriors have a chance of stopping  aaron by themselves anyway as he goes to  kill one of the engineers ambassador  kiyomi leaps out of her chair and the  scene pans out to a point where we just  hear three gunshots the sound of these  shots lets everyone in the port know  that something isn't right and in the  room flock is getting whooped by a  middle-aged woman some more jaegers then  burst in after hearing the gunshots but  before they can kill kyomi mikasa  crashes through the window and deals  with both of them we know that flock  already had his own suspicions about her  so after seeing this betrayal he  clumsily uses his gear to break out and  lets his soldiers know the situation  this leads to an instant reaction with  many of the aegis swooping in to blow up  the room and mikasa only barely makes it  out as the explosion throws her into a  wall  on the stairs the azimutha were then  confronted by more soldiers but these  ones were killed by hanji and magath  who's now ditched his malian uniform in  favor of the survey called jacket their  mission right now is to get everyone  into the basement so that reiner and  annie can go wild with their titans  without needing to worry about  collateral damage before we get into  that though down by the flying boat a  panic dazz goes to reconnect the  explosives as armin tries to step in  samuel then brutally shoots him in the  drawer chest and stomach but part of the  reason he did this was because armin has  shifter abilities his colossal titan  means that he's able to survive injuries  like this which is why he ended up  getting shot while connie managed to  avoid the same treatment having realized  that they've been betrayed samuel is  seriously hurt by this and starts to cry  as he reminisces about this memory back  in season 1. back then sasha had stolen  some meat from one of their superior  offices but her reasoning was that once  they capture more land from the titans  there'll be even more meat to go around  following that samuel and connie agreed  with this and they were the first ones  to ask for some of the michi stole and  you can tell that since then samuel  never imagined that they'd be in a  scenario like this  switching back to the azmobito they were  hiding at the bottom of this staircase  as the aegiris continued to bombard the  entrance with thunderspears them being  underground gave reiner and annie the  freedom they needed to go wild and this  sequence of her using the odm gear was  by far one of the best cuts of the  episode the fact she hadn't practiced  for four years made this even more  impressive than it already was and the  warriors pull up behind flock to  manifest their titans  next to the flying boat this titan  lightning catches samuel by surprise and  while he's distracted connie uses it as  a chance to tackle him meanwhile over by  the rocks the rest of the alliance was  observing with the captain having woken  up just in time to watch the show  the female and armored titans then  manifest soon after this and the jaegris  rampage that annie had been asking for  finally gets underway  when it comes to connie he and samuel  were fighting over possession of the gun  while daz continued to reconnect the  explosives zombie armin then muscles up  the strength to lunge at him cause like  we've established under no circumstances  can the alliance allow the ship to be  destroyed  eventually they get into a situation  where daz has a gun to his head but when  you take into account his personality in  my opinion there was a pretty low chance  that he was ever gonna pull the trigger  that being said a low chance doesn't  mean it's impossible and an injury to  the brain like this could be fatal even  for him obviously we've seen that rhino  has survived worse but in those  situations he was able to transfer his  consciousness which isn't something the  army is known to be aware of i think  it's fair to say that in this moment  armin was leaving his fate in daz's  hands and over to the side samuel tries  to understand why this is happening from  his perspective this whole betrayal must  be super confusing because they've been  fighting for the same goal their whole  lives and now all of a sudden connie and  army are switching sides to save people  that hate them this is when armin  flashes back to something bertolt said  when he betrayed them which is that  someone has to be the person to stain  their hands with blood in berto's case  he hated himself for having to kill  people but he did what he had to do  because he didn't really have another  choice  similarly armin and kony are now in  pretty much the exact same situation  because they didn't want to kill anyone  and they made that pretty clear but now  they've been forced into a corner where  they have to choose between daz and  samuel's life or the lives of millions  of innocent people ultimately connie  chooses the latter and this scene was  done incredibly well because he shoots  daz and then slowly realizes what he has  to do next in the 