ir  mission right now is to get everyone  into the basement so that reiner and  annie can go wild with their titans  without needing to worry about  collateral damage before we get into  that though down by the flying boat a  panic dazz goes to reconnect the  explosives as armin tries to step in  samuel then brutally shoots him in the  drawer chest and stomach but part of the  reason he did this was because armin has  shifter abilities his colossal titan  means that he's able to survive injuries  like this which is why he ended up  getting shot while connie managed to  avoid the same treatment having realized  that they've been betrayed samuel is  seriously hurt by this and starts to cry  as he reminisces about this memory back  in season 1. back then sasha had stolen  some meat from one of their superior  offices but her reasoning was that once  they capture more land from the titans  there'll be even more meat to go around  following that samuel and connie agreed  with this and they were the first ones  to ask for some of the michi stole and  you can tell that since then samuel  never imagined that they'd be in a  scenario like this  switching back to the azmobito they were  hiding at the bottom of this staircase  as the aegiris continued to bombard the  entrance with thunderspears them being  underground gave reiner and annie the  freedom they needed to go wild and this  sequence of her using the odm gear was  by far one of the best cuts of the  episode the fact she hadn't practiced  for four years made this even more  impressive than it already was and the  warriors pull up behind flock to  manifest their titans  next to the flying boat this titan  lightning catches samuel by surprise and  while he's distracted connie uses it as  a chance to tackle him meanwhile over by  the rocks the rest of the alliance was  observing with the captain having woken  up just in time to watch the show  the female and armored titans then  manifest soon after this and the jaegris  rampage that annie had been asking for  finally gets underway  when it comes to connie he and samuel  were fighting over possession of the gun  while daz continued to reconnect the  explosives zombie armin then muscles up  the strength to lunge at him cause like  we've established under no circumstances  can the alliance allow the ship to be  destroyed  eventually they get into a situation  where daz has a gun to his head but when  you take into account his personality in  my opinion there was a pretty low chance  that he was ever gonna pull the trigger  that being said a low chance doesn't  mean it's impossible and an injury to  the brain like this could be fatal even  for him obviously we've seen that rhino  has survived worse but in those  situations he was able to transfer his  consciousness which isn't something the  army is known to be aware of i think  it's fair to say that in this moment  armin was leaving his fate in daz's  hands and over to the side samuel tries  to understand why this is happening from  his perspective this whole betrayal must  be super confusing because they've been  fighting for the same goal their whole  lives and now all of a sudden connie and  army are switching sides to save people  that hate them this is when armin  flashes back to something bertolt said  when he betrayed them which is that  someone has to be the person to stain  their hands with blood in berto's case  he hated himself for having to kill  people but he did what he had to do  because he didn't really have another  choice  similarly armin and kony are now in  pretty much the exact same situation  because they didn't want to kill anyone  and they made that pretty clear but now  they've been forced into a corner where  they have to choose between daz and  samuel's life or the lives of millions  of innocent people ultimately connie  chooses the latter and this scene was  done incredibly well because he shoots  daz and then slowly realizes what he has  to do next in the manga version it  seemed like he just killed daz and then  instantly shot samuel but the anime does  it way better because you can really see  how conflicted he was in this moment  the episode ends with the haunting shot  of connie screaming over his friend's  dead body proving just how far he's  willing to go to stop the rumbling  anyway people that was my breakdown for  episode 26 of attack on titan season 4  and if it helped your understanding of  the episode in any way then be sure to  hit that sub button for more videos like  this  finally as a quick thank you for those  of you who stuck around to the end i've  been working on my newest installment of  what if erin got the colossal titan the  new video will pick up immediately after  the last part left off with the  warhammer titan confronting the scouts  in liberio from there it spirals into an  all-out war that covers literally the  entire malian continent and one of my  intentions was to show how everyone  would see the weaknesses in mali that  could have been exploited in the process  there will be characters on both sides  we have to make hard decisions and the  second half of the video will be all  about how the world reacts to these  events  all the artwork and the script is now  fully complete and it's a pretty long  script so um i'm hoping to record it all  next week and maybe get the video out by  wednesday or thursday but if i can't get  out on those days then it will be coming  out probably the monday or tuesday of  the following week  if you've watched this far then i'm  assuming you're a fan of the series so i  would say that you should turn on your  notifications so you don't miss it  because you know this is in my opinion  my best ever video so i'm trying to make  it perfect i want everything to be you  know i want the editing to be good as  well so um yeah when it comes out be  sure to have notifications on so you  don't miss it  thanks for watching as always and until  the next one peace out
 

